    <string name="act_me1_title">Vinegar Glucose Buffer</string>
    <string name="act_me1_ipre">1 tbsp Apple Cider Vinegar in 250ml water before your largest meal.</string>
    <string name="act_me1_bio">Acetic acid inhibits alpha-amylase, slowing the breakdown of starch into glucose.</string>
    <string name="act_me1_phys">Reduces post-prandial glucose spike by up to 30%%, preserving insulin sensitivity.</string>
    <string name="act_me1_rsch">Clinical trials show that acetic acid significantly blunts the glycemic response when consumed 2-5 minutes before a carbohydrate load.</string>
    <string name="act_me2_title">Post-Prandial Glycemic Walk</string>
    <string name="act_me2_ipre">15-minute brisk walk immediately following a meal.</string>
    <string name="act_me2_bio">Muscular contraction recruits GLUT4 transporters to the cell surface without requiring high insulin.</string>
    <string name="act_me2_phys">Clears glucose from the bloodstream rapidly, preventing glycation of proteins.</string>
    <string name="act_me2_rsch">Even a short walk is significantly more effective at glucose clearance than standing or sitting after a meal.</string>
    <string name="act_co1_title">NSDR (Non-Sleep Deep Rest)</string>
    <string name="act_co1_ipre">20 minutes of guided NSDR or Yoga Nidra.</string>
    <string name="act_co1_bio">Shifts the brain from high-frequency beta waves to alpha/theta waves without sleep.</string>
    <string name="act_co1_phys">Replenishes acetylcholine levels in the prefrontal cortex, enhancing neuroplasticity.</string>
    <string name="act_co1_rsch">NSDR has been shown to increase dopamine levels in the nigrostriatal pathway by up to 65%%.</string>
    <string name="act_ph1_title">Passive Hanging Protocol</string>
    <string name="act_ph1_ipre">Perform 3x30s passive dead-hangs from a pull-up bar.</string>
    <string name="act_ph1_bio">Decompresses the intervertebral discs and increases subacromial space in the shoulders.</string>
    <string name="act_ph1_phys">Reverses the compressive effects of gravity and sedentary behavior on the spine.</string>
    <string name="act_ph1_rsch">Regular hanging is a foundational practice for maintaining shoulder mobility and spinal health into late age.</string>
    <string name="act_ph2_title">CARS (Controlled Articular Rotations)</string>
    <string name="act_ph2_ipre">Perform full-range rotations for neck, shoulders, and hips.</string>
    <string name="act_ph2_bio">Stimulates mechanoreceptors in the joint capsule and ensures synovial fluid distribution.</string>
    <string name="act_ph2_phys">Prevents joint "locking" and maintains the "use it or lose it" range of motion.</string>
    <string name="act_ph2_rsch">CARS are a daily maintenance requirement to map the joint workspace in the central nervous system.</string>
    <string name="act_sl1_title">Immediate Wake Activation</string>
    <string name="act_sl1_ipre">Exit bed within 120 seconds of waking.</string>
    <string name="act_sl1_bio">Signals the brain to terminate sleep state and initiates Cortisol Awakening Response (CAR).</string>
    <string name="act_sl1_phys">Prevents sleep inertia and resets metabolic clock for daily energy stability.</string>
    <string name="act_sl1_rsch">Execute by placing your alarm device </string>
    <string name="act_sl2_title">SCN Photobiomodulation</string>
    <string name="act_sl2_ipre">15m of bright natural light exposure.</string>
    <string name="act_sl2_bio">Light triggers Suprachiasmatic Nucleus (SCN) to suppress melatonin and set the 16h timer for nocturnal release.</string>
    <string name="act_sl2_phys">Essential for long-term circadian stability and prevention of seasonal affective disorders.</string>
    <string name="act_sl2_rsch">Prioritize direct outdoor exposure without windows or sunglasses. If overcast, extend to 30m. This lux intensity is necessary to saturate melanopsin-containing retinal ganglion cells that govern your master clock.</string>
    <string name="act_sl3_title">Melatonin Shield: Blue Light Fast</string>
    <string name="act_sl3_ipre">Apply red filter to all screens or use blockers 120m before sleep.</string>
    <string name="act_sl3_bio">Protects melanopsin-containing ganglion cells. Melatonin is a potent anti-carcinogenic antioxidant.</string>
    <string name="act_sl3_phys">Maximizes nocturnal anti-cancer mechanisms and cellular repair.</string>
    <string name="act_sl3_rsch">Apply \'Night Shift\' software and physical amber-tinted lenses. Even low-intensity blue light can suppress melatonin release for up to 90 minutes. Ensure all peripheral LEDs in the bedroom are covered or disabled.</string>
    <string name="act_sl4_title">Glymphatic Thermal Trigger</string>
    <string name="act_sl4_ipre">Lower bedroom temperature to 18�C (64�F).</string>
    <string name="act_sl4_bio">A drop in core body temperature is the primary physiological trigger for entering N3 Deep Sleep.</string>
    <string name="act_sl4_phys">Triggers glymphatic system to \'flush\' beta-amyloid, reducing Alzheimer\'s and dementia risk.</string>
    <string name="act_sl4_rsch">Combine with a warm shower 90m before bed. The \'rebound\' vasodilation in hands and feet facilitates the necessary 1�C drop in core temperature required for neural waste-clearance cycles.</string>
    <string name="act_ca1_title">Orthostatic Vascular Priming</string>
    <string name="act_ca1_ipre">Stand up immediately and perform 2m of light stretching.</string>
    <string name="act_ca1_bio">Forces the vascular system to adapt to gravity, stimulating nitric oxide release in the endothelium.</string>
    <string name="act_ca1_phys">Improves vascular compliance and reduces risk of orthostatic hypertension.</string>
    <string name="act_ca1_rsch">Perform slow, controlled reaches toward the ceiling while breathing deeply. This mechanical stretching of large vessels increases shear stress on vessel walls, inducing eNOS activity.</string>
    <string name="act_osmotic_title">Osmotic Loading</string>
    <string name="act_osmotic_why">Alcohol suppresses vasopressin, causing massive dehydration. Electrolytes are required to restore osmotic pressure.</string>
    <string name="act_osmotic_what">250ml water, sipped slowly every 20 seconds.</string>
    <string name="act_osmotic_outcome">Stabilized cellular hydration and reduced post-alcohol brain fog.</string>
    <string name="act_osmotic_prep_title">Preparation</string>
    <string name="act_osmotic_prep_desc">Get 250ml water + electrolytes.</string>
    <string name="act_osmotic_sip_title">Osmotic Sips</string>
    <string name="act_osmotic_sip_desc">Slow sips every 20s for mucosal absorption.</string>
    <string name="act_osmotic_impact">Hydration complete. Osmotic pressure stabilized. Liver filtration capacity increased by ~12%.</string>
    <string name="act_pulmonary_title">Pulmonary Expansion</string>
    <string name="act_pulmonary_why">Smoking reduces functional lung volume. Diaphragmatic breathing re-engages the lower lobes.</string>
    <string name="act_pulmonary_what">Slow, deep belly breaths through the nose.</string>
    <string name="act_pulmonary_outcome">Increased VO2 efficiency and reduced systemic vascular tension.</string>
    <string name="act_pulmonary_posture_title">Posture</string>
    <string name="act_pulmonary_posture_desc">Sit upright, hand on belly.</string>
    <string name="act_pulmonary_ritual_title">Ritual</string>
    <string name="act_pulmonary_ritual_desc">Deep belly inhale, slow exhale.</string>
    <string name="act_pulmonary_impact">Lung capacity engaged. Oxygen saturation improved. Residual CO2 offloaded.</string>
    <string name="act_vagal_title">Vagal Nerve Strike</string>
    <string name="act_vagal_why">Cold exposure triggers the Mammalian Dive Reflex, immediately activating the parasympathetic branch.</string>
    <string name="act_vagal_what">Apply cold water to the face/neck for 60 seconds.</string>
    <string name="act_vagal_outcome">Immediate reduction in cortisol and resting heart rate.</string>
    <string name="act_vagal_cold_title">Cold Exposure</string>
    <string name="act_vagal_cold_desc">Splash face with cold water or use an ice pack on neck.</string>
    <string name="act_vagal_impact">Nervous system regulated. Vagal tone improved. Heart rate stabilized.</string>
    <string name="act_hepatic_title">Hepatic Phase II Load</string>
    <string name="act_hepatic_why">Alcohol creates acetaldehyde. Phase II liver detox requires specific sulfur-containing compounds (NAC/Glutathione) to neutralize toxins.</string>
    <string name="act_hepatic_what">Take NAC or eat broccoli sprouts with water.</string>
    <string name="act_hepatic_outcome">Accelerated clearance of toxic alcohol byproducts and reduced liver strain.</string>
    <string name="act_hepatic_loading_title">Nutrient Loading</string>
    <string name="act_hepatic_loading_desc">Consume Cruciferous extracts or NAC with 200ml water.</string>
    <string name="act_hepatic_impact">Phase II detoxification pathways primed. Glutathione precursors acknowledged.</string>
    <string name="act_steam_title">Mucolytic Steam Protocol</string>
    <string name="act_steam_why">Nicotine paralyzes the cilia in your lungs. Steam helps thin the mucus, making it easier to expectorate tar.</string>
    <string name="act_steam_what">Inhale steam from a bowl of hot water or a humidifier.</string>
    <string name="act_steam_outcome">Improved pulmonary clearance and reduced smoker\'s cough.</string>
    <string name="act_steam_inhale_title">Steam Inhalation</string>
    <string name="act_steam_inhale_desc">Inhale warm steam for deep bronchial reach.</string>
    <string name="act_steam_impact">Tar-laden mucus thinned. Bronchial pathways moisturized.</string>
    <string name="act_thiamine_title">Thiamine Saturation Ritual</string>
    <string name="act_thiamine_why">Alcohol severely inhibits Thiamine (B1) absorption, which is critical for brain energy. Deficiency leads to neurological decline.</string>
    <string name="act_thiamine_what">Take B1 supplement with a full glass of water.</string>
    <string name="act_thiamine_outcome">Protection of Wernicke-Korsakoff pathways and improved cognitive clarity.</string>
    <string name="act_thiamine_intake_title">Oral Intake</string>
    <string name="act_thiamine_intake_desc">Take 100mg Thiamine with water.</string>
    <string name="act_thiamine_impact">B1 levels stabilized. Cerebral glucose metabolism protected.</string>
    <string name="act_inspiratory_title">Inspiratory Muscle Training</string>
    <string name="act_inspiratory_why">Smoking weakens the primary respiratory muscles. Resistance training restores diaphragm power.</string>
    <string name="act_inspiratory_what">Inhale deeply, then exhale through a small opening in your lips, creating resistance.</string>
    <string name="act_inspiratory_outcome">Reduced breathlessness and improved thoracic mobility.</string>
    <string name="act_inspiratory_res_title">Resistance</string>
    <string name="act_inspiratory_res_desc">Breathe through pursed lips with moderate force.</string>
    <string name="act_inspiratory_impact">Diaphragm strength increased. Accessory breathing muscles recruited.</string>
    <string name="act_coherence_title">Heart-Rate Coherence</string>
    <string name="act_coherence_why">Smoking and alcohol both increase resting HR. Coherence breathing trains the heart to oscillate in a healthy, regenerative pattern.</string>
    <string name="act_coherence_what">Follow the visual for a perfectly timed 4-6 rhythm.</string>
    <string name="act_coherence_outcome">Lowered systolic blood pressure and improved HRV.</string>
    <string name="act_coherence_step_title">Coherence</string>
    <string name="act_coherence_step_desc">4s inhale, 6s exhale. Smooth transition.</string>
    <string name="act_coherence_impact">Autonomic balance reached. HRV increased. Cardiac load reduced.</string>
    <string name="act_postural_title">Postural Drainage Protocol</string>
    <string name="act_postural_why">Gravity helps move tar and mucus from the lower lung segments to the larger airways for clearance.</string>
    <string name="act_postural_what">Use pillows to prop up your hips while lying on your front.</string>
    <string name="act_postural_outcome">Deep lung clearance and improved oxygenation in the base of the lungs.</string>
    <string name="act_postural_pos_title">Positioning</string>
    <string name="act_postural_pos_desc">Lie with chest lower than hips. Breathe deep.</string>
    <string name="act_postural_impact">Lower lung lobes cleared. Gravity-assisted mucus mobilization.</string>
    <string name="act_reset_title">Parasympathetic Reset</string>
    <string name="act_reset_why">Alcohol disrupts sleep architecture. 4-7-8 breathing is a biological \'off-switch\' for the sympathetic nervous system.</string>
    <string name="act_reset_what">Inhale through nose (4s), hold (7s), exhale through mouth (8s).Log completion to update neural markers.</string>
    <string name="act_reset_outcome">Rapid induction of the relaxation response for restorative sleep.</string>
    <string name="act_reset_cycle_title">4-7-8 Cycle</string>
    <string name="act_reset_cycle_desc">Inhale 4, Hold 7, Exhale 8.</string>
    <string name="act_reset_impact">CNS down-regulated. Melatonin readiness optimized.</string>
    <string name="act_sigh_title">Neural Reset (Sigh)</string>
    <string name="act_sigh_why">Fastest biological way to down-regulate. Pops open collapsed alveoli.</string>
    <string name="act_sigh_what">Double inhale + long, audile sigh.</string>
    <string name="act_sigh_outcome">Shift from Sympathetic (fight/flight) to Parasympathetic dominance.</string>
    <string name="act_sigh_cycle_title">Cycle</string>
    <string name="act_sigh_cycle_desc">Double inhale, long exhale.</string>
    <string name="act_sigh_impact">Vagal tone increased. Amygdala reactivity lowered.</string>
    <string name="act_surfing_title">Neural Wave Navigation</string>
    <string name="act_surfing_why">Cravings are neurochemical pulses. Observing them as waves prevents addiction loop reinforcement.</string>
    <string name="act_surfing_what">Mindful observation of physical sensations in the throat/chest.</string>
    <string name="act_surfing_outcome">Dopamine baseline recalibration and increased prefrontal control.</string>
    <string name="act_surfing_step_title">Surfing</string>
    <string name="act_surfing_step_desc">Observe the physical sensation without judgment.</string>
    <string name="act_surfing_impact">Craving wave navigated. Addiction neural pathways weakened.</string>
    <string name="act_circadian_title">Circadian Rhythm Lock</string>
    <string name="act_circadian_why">Alcohol and nicotine fragment sleep architecture by suppressing REM and increasing core temperature. This ritual recalibrates the master clock.</string>
    <string name="act_circadian_what">Follow the light pulse to signal the SCN (Suprachiasmatic Nucleus) for melatonin readiness.</string>
    <string name="act_circadian_outcome">Improved sleep continuity and stabilized circadian signaling.</string>
    <string name="act_circadian_step_title">SCN Sync</string>
    <string name="act_circadian_step_desc">Match your gaze to the central light pulse. Dim environment required.</string>
    <string name="act_circadian_impact">Circadian markers updated. Biological clock synchronized.</string>
    <string name="act_dopamine_title">Dopamine Receptor Reset</string>
    <string name="act_dopamine_why">Chronic substance use down-regulates D2 receptors. This ritual uses sensory-minimum stimuli to allow receptor sensitivity to return.</string>
    <string name="act_dopamine_what">Focus on the singular point. Minimize all other sensory input. This allows reward circuits to cool down.</string>
    <string name="act_dopamine_outcome">Restoration of prefrontal control and reduced impulse volatility.</string>
    <string name="act_dopamine_step_title">Sensory Minimum</string>
    <string name="act_dopamine_step_desc">Gaze at the pulse. Acknowledge and release external sensory noise.</string>
    <string name="act_dopamine_impact">Reward circuit baseline reset. Prefrontal engagement increased.</string>
    <string name="act_st1_title">Acute Neural Reset (Sigh)</string>
    <string name="act_st1_ipre">5 reps of \'Physiological Sigh\' (double inhale, long exhale).</string>
    <string name="act_st1_bio">Rapidly offloads CO2 from blood, triggering a vagal signal to slow heart rate.</string>
    <string name="act_st1_phys">Immediate down-regulation of the sympathetic (fight/flight) nervous system.</string>
    <string name="act_st1_rsch">Inhale through nose until lungs are 90%% full, then take a second sharp inhale to pop open the alveoli. Exhale through mouth for double the length of inhale. This is the fastest way to lower HR.</string>
